From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yewsifofficial <yewsifofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:48:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nextendo: say where the game gives up, and stop the capture
 cutting the login short

Measured against the working emulator's trace of the same minute, with both
logs now stamped. Everything that can be counted agrees: the same twenty
probes and ten replies on the same two responders, the same park and adopt,
the same peer handed over, and neither client receives a single datagram on
the play socket between adopting it and deciding what to do. The emulator
then polls that empty socket for 962 ms and reaches the peer. This engine
abandons the session 467 microseconds after the third probe, having made no
socket call in between. Nothing it was given differs, so Pia is reading
state of its own and taking another branch.

The gate placed by offset cannot say where: its own line admits the caller
it reports lies outside every module, so its address is wrong for this
build. nn::err::ErrorResultVariant is called by the game itself with a real
return address, and it is already where 2618-0578 is read. So the first few
Pia failures recorded there now carry a backtrace, which names the module
and offset the session was abandoned at. Only Pia's own module and only four
of them: the game records ordinary results here constantly while all is
well.

The frame capture was also cutting the one message that matters in half. The
login frame is about 1,250 bytes and the capture held 640, so the 1,145-byte
ID token inside it lay outside what the decoder could see and was reported
missing -- a fault in this engine's logging, not in the login. The capture
is now 2,048 bytes.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (online play is out of nxnative's scope)
Reason: Nextendo online play for Super Smash Bros. Ultimate
Issue: yewsiff/NX2Apple (no tracker: issues are disabled on this fork)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017xdHQoEipBX2wTqN8BNnMv
---
 dm/host/hle_offline.c        | 11 ++++++++++-
 dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_offline.c b/dm/host/hle_offline.c
index df41eff..eca9f33 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_offline.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_offline.c
@@ -221,8 +221,17 @@ static void *err_variant_pass(void *v, const uint32_t *a, const char *sym, void
     static _Atomic uint64_t last;   // the game records the same ordinary result over and over while all is well; a run of one code is logged once
     uint64_t this = (uint64_t)code << 62 | (uint64_t)w1 << 32 | w0;
     if ((w0 || w1) && dm_net_online() && atomic_exchange(&last, this) != this && atomic_fetch_add(&n, 1) < 200) {
+        unsigned mod = code ? w0 : 2000 + (w0 & 0x1ff), desc = code ? w1 : (w0 >> 9) & 0x1fff;
         if (code) NXLOGA("the game records a failure: error code %04u-%04u", w0, w1);
-        else NXLOGA("the game records a failure: result %#x = %04u-%04u", w0, 2000 + (w0 & 0x1ff), (w0 >> 9) & 0x1fff);
+        else NXLOGA("the game records a failure: result %#x = %04u-%04u", w0, mod, desc);
+        // Pia keeps its own results to itself and gives up without a word, so where it gave up is the one thing left to learn. This call has a
+        // real return address, unlike the gate placed by offset, so the frames above it name the module and offset Pia abandoned the session at.
+        // Only the first few, and only for Pia's own module (2618): the game records ordinary results here constantly while all is well
+        static _Atomic int bt;
+        if (mod == 2618 && atomic_fetch_add(&bt, 1) < 4) {
+            NXLOGA("where the game gave up on %04u-%04u (innermost first):", mod, desc);
+            dm_backtrace((uint64_t)__builtin_frame_address(0));
+        }
     }
     if (*orig) return (*orig)(v, a);
     if (v) { uint32_t *o = v; o[0] = code ? 2 : 1; o[1] = w0; if (code) o[2] = w1; }   // (no definition to call: the Result form as above, the ErrorCode form by the next state)
diff --git a/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m b/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
index 254f42c..4f953e8 100644
--- a/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
+++ b/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
@@ -652,7 +652,7 @@ static int trust_matches_pin(sec_trust_t trust, const char *sni) {
     uint64_t sent, got;
     NSMutableData *rhead;     // the server's HTTP head until its blank line
     int rhead_done, nframes[2];
-    struct { int have; uint8_t h[14]; uint64_t skip, len; int op, masked; uint8_t mask[4]; unsigned pos, capn; uint8_t cap[640]; } ws[2];   // 0: game → server, 1: server → game
+    struct { int have; uint8_t h[14]; uint64_t skip, len; int op, masked; uint8_t mask[4]; unsigned pos, capn; uint8_t cap[2048]; } ws[2];   // 2048: the login frame is about 1,250 bytes, and at 640 the ID token inside it fell outside the capture and was reported missing   // 0: game → server, 1: server → game
     int nnex, split[2];       // NEX calls logged so far; a split NEX message is passing in this direction
     NSMutableData *cbody[2];  // a close frame's body while it passes
     NSString *wsproto;        // the WebSocket subprotocol the game's request asks for ("NEX"); the server's answer must name it
